window.__LDNDRC_PAGES = Object.assign(window.__LDNDRC_PAGES || {}, {"uiux-principles":"<p>The student UI deliberately rejects the floating-window &quot;cockpit&quot; desktop metaphor. Students are here to learn ROS, not to arrange windows.</p>\n<h2 id=\"five-principles\">Five principles</h2><ol>\n<li><strong>Focus over window management.</strong> One active tool fills the stage; switching is instant and keeps the others alive.</li>\n<li><strong>Split view is a mode, not freeform drag.</strong> Exactly three layouts: Code, Sim, Code | Sim.</li>\n<li><strong>Status is ambient.</strong> <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">Session</span> state lives in the top bar on every screen, not on a polling page.</li>\n<li><strong>Desktop is an escape hatch.</strong> It opens in its own tab, as a secondary action.</li>\n<li><strong>Light-on-dark mission control.</strong> Warm, high contrast, built for long <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">sessions</span>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"the-test-for-any-new-screen\">The test for any new screen</h2><p>Does it answer <em>where am I</em>, <em>is my workspace ready</em>, and <em>what can I do now</em>? If a screen answers only two, it is not finished.</p>\n<h2 id=\"check-it-yourself\">Check it yourself</h2><p>Open the launch screen and count the primary actions. There should be exactly one.</p>","student-spa":"<p>The student web app is a small state machine with a route for each state. It is React 18 and Vite, served as static assets by the Go panel.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-routes\">The routes</h2><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Route</th>\n<th>Screen</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>/login</code></td>\n<td>sign in</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/launch</code></td>\n<td>workspace status, Launch/Stop, tool cards</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/app?view=code</code></td>\n<td><span class=\"term\" data-term=\"code-server\" tabindex=\"0\">code-server</span> fills the stage</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/app?view=sim</code></td>\n<td><span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gzweb\" tabindex=\"0\">gzweb</span> fills the stage</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/app?view=split</code></td>\n<td>code and sim side by side</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>/desktop</code></td>\n<td>Selkies, own tab</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"the-state-machine\">The state machine</h2><div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"text\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">text</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-text\">LOGGED_OUT → LOGGED_IN → NO_SESSION → PROVISIONING → READY ⇄ STOPPING → STOPPED\n                              ↑                          ↓\n                              └──────── ERROR ───────────┘</code></pre></div><p>Every state has exactly one primary action. That constraint is what keeps the UI from growing a dashboard nobody reads — see <a href=\"#/uiux-principles\" class=\"topic-link\">Focus over window management</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"check-it-yourself\">Check it yourself</h2><div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8082/ | <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">head</span> -5</code></pre></div>","instructor-console":"<p>Before the console existed, approving a laptop meant a <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"jwt\" tabindex=\"0\">JWT</span>, a curl command, and a <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"node\" tabindex=\"0\">node</span> ID copied out of JSON. The instructor console puts that on a screen.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-it-does\">What it does</h2><ul>\n<li>Lists pending join requests with hardware details.</li>\n<li>Approves or denies with a reason.</li>\n<li>Shows the live download counter from the onboarding portal.</li>\n<li>Distinguishes approved from joined, so a laptop that never connected is visible.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"why-it-matters\">Why it matters</h2><p>Approval is the security boundary of the whole onboarding path — see <a href=\"#/nodes-api\" class=\"topic-link\">Register, approve, poll</a>. If only one person can perform it, and that person needs a shell, the workshop is one forgotten token away from stalling.</p>\n<h2 id=\"check-it-yourself\">Check it yourself</h2><p>Open <code>control.ros-platform.local/admin</code> with an <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"operator\" tabindex=\"0\">operator</span> login and confirm a pending request appears after <code>POST /api/nodes/register</code>.</p>"});
